SIMPLE  =                    T / conforms to FITS standard                      BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    0 / number of array dimensions                     EXTEND  =                    T                                                  SURVEY  = 'DESI    '                                                            DR      = 'DR1     '                                                            ABSORBER= 'CIV     '           / Absorber name                                  KERWIDTH= '[3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]' / Kernel width in pixels (ker_width_pixels)      COEFFSIG=                    2 / sigma threshold (coeff_sigma)                  MULTRE  =                    1 / Multiplicative factor for residuals (mult_resi)D_PIX   =                  0.6 / tolerance for line separation (in Ang) (d_pix) PM_PIXEL=                  100 / N_Pixel for noise estimation (pm_pixel)        SN_LINE1=                    3 / S/N threshold for first line (sn_line1)        SN_LINE2=                    2 / S/N threshold for second line (sn_line2)       EWCOVAR =                    F / Use covariance for EW error (use_covariance)   LOGWAVE =                    T / Use log wavelength scaling (logwave)           LAM_ESEP=                   25 / lambda edges to avoid edges (lam_edge_sep)     BLUE_LAM=               1310.0 / blue end of quasar-rest frame (Ang) for search RED_LAM =              1549.48 / red end of quasar-rest frame (Ang) for search  CONTERR =                 0.05 / fractional error in continuum normalization    CONFLEV =                 0.95 / minimum confidence level for selection         N_METHOD= 'AODM    '           / Column Density Method: apparent optical depth  DELTA_V =                  300 / +/- velocity (km/s) to calculate optical depth NUMPY   = '1.21.6  '           / numpy version                                  ASTROPY = '5.1     '           / astropy version                                SCIPY   = '1.9.1   '           / scipy version                                  NUMBA   = '0.55.1  '           / numba version                                  QSOABFI = '2.1.0   '           / qsoabsfind version                             MATPLOT = '3.5.2   '           / matplotlib version                             EXTNAME = 'PRIMARY '                                                            END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             XTENSION= 'BINTABLE'           / binary table extension                         BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    2 / number of array dimensions                     NAXIS1  =                  208 / length of dimension 1                          NAXIS2  =                   21 / length of dimension 2                          PCOUNT  =                    0 / number of group parameters                     GCOUNT  =                    1 / number of groups                               TFIELDS =                   16 / number of table fields                         TTYPE1  = 'INDEX_SPEC'                                                          TFORM1  = 'K       '                                                            TTYPE2  = 'Z_ABS   '                                                            TFORM2  = 'D       '                                                            TTYPE3  = 'GAUSS_FIT'                                                           TFORM3  = '6D      '                                                            